      "content": "i was reading about the heat death of the universe and how everything just eventually reaches this state of maximum entropy where nothing happens anymore... no energy, no change, just empty stillness. it's kind of haunting. honestly it feels a lot like my own life lately. just this constant, exhausting struggle to keep things moving when it feels like everything is just sliding toward nothingness anyway. what's even the point of fighting the decay when the end result is always just zero?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
